[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":790},["ShallowReactive",2],{"article-jq-json-outline":3,"articles-100":667,"articles-10":769},{"id":4,"title":5,"alt":6,"body":7,"description":650,"extension":651,"image":652,"meta":653,"navigation":654,"ogImage":655,"path":656,"postDate":657,"published":658,"robots":655,"schemaOrg":655,"seo":659,"sitemap":660,"stem":661,"tags":662,"updated":655,"url":655,"__hash__":666},"blog\u002Fblog\u002Fjq-json-outline.md","Quickly outline large JSON responses with a custom jq function","Abstract image representing the essence of json structure",{"type":8,"value":9,"toc":642},"minimark",[10,14,34,37,42,45,129,132,136,139,295,302,306,309,367,370,489,496,500,503,570,574,577,599,602,631,635,638],[11,12,13],"p",{},"I was recently digging into Immich’s API to see if it exposes the fields I needed for some details about my photos. Immich is my self-hosted photo-management service. The API returned hundreds of lines of JSON. I just wanted to see its structure to check the fields I needed, but scrolling through all that data felt slow. I did what any sane programmer would do: I spent even more time trying to automate it.",[11,15,16,17,24,25,29,30,33],{},"I’ve used ",[18,19,23],"a",{"href":20,"rel":21},"https:\u002F\u002Fjqlang.org\u002F",[22],"nofollow","jq"," before for quick JSON tweaks (it’s basically ",[26,27,28],"code",{},"sed"," or ",[26,31,32],{},"awk"," for JSON), so I wondered if it could help here. A quick search showed that jq can collapse arrays to a single-item preview, then recurse through the whole document for a clean outline of the JSON’s shape in one pass.",[11,35,36],{},"I later found out the response structures are already listed in the Immich API docs. I could have just looked that up and saved myself the hassle. But hey, it could well have been an endpoint with no docs, and my method works for any JSON API response.",[38,39,41],"h2",{"id":40},"the-jq-function","The jq function",[11,43,44],{},"Here’s the jq function I came up with. You can run it in a terminal:",[46,47,52],"pre",{"className":48,"code":49,"language":50,"meta":51,"style":51},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","jq '\ndef shape:\n  if type == \"array\" then\n    if length > 0 then [ (.[0] | shape) ] else [] end\n  elif type == \"object\" then\n    with_entries(.value |= shape)\n  else\n    type\n  end;\nshape\n' response.json\n","bash","",[26,53,54,66,72,78,84,90,96,102,108,114,120],{"__ignoreMap":51},[55,56,59,62],"span",{"class":57,"line":58},"line",1,[55,60,23],{"class":61},"sScJk",[55,63,65],{"class":64},"sZZnC"," '\n",[55,67,69],{"class":57,"line":68},2,[55,70,71],{"class":64},"def shape:\n",[55,73,75],{"class":57,"line":74},3,[55,76,77],{"class":64},"  if type == \"array\" then\n",[55,79,81],{"class":57,"line":80},4,[55,82,83],{"class":64},"    if length > 0 then [ (.[0] | shape) ] else [] end\n",[55,85,87],{"class":57,"line":86},5,[55,88,89],{"class":64},"  elif type == \"object\" then\n",[55,91,93],{"class":57,"line":92},6,[55,94,95],{"class":64},"    with_entries(.value |= shape)\n",[55,97,99],{"class":57,"line":98},7,[55,100,101],{"class":64},"  else\n",[55,103,105],{"class":57,"line":104},8,[55,106,107],{"class":64},"    type\n",[55,109,111],{"class":57,"line":110},9,[55,112,113],{"class":64},"  end;\n",[55,115,117],{"class":57,"line":116},10,[55,118,119],{"class":64},"shape\n",[55,121,123,126],{"class":57,"line":122},11,[55,124,125],{"class":64},"'",[55,127,128],{"class":64}," response.json\n",[11,130,131],{},"The function checks each value. If it's an array, keep just the first item and recurse. If it's an object, walk through each key and recurse into the value. If it's a primitive like a string or number, return just the type name.",[38,133,135],{"id":134},"actual-immich-api-shape","Actual Immich API shape",[11,137,138],{},"Here's a simplified output of the jq function applied to the Immich API response:",[46,140,144],{"className":141,"code":142,"language":143,"meta":51,"style":51},"language-json shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","{\n  \"albums\": {\n    \"count\": \"number\",\n    ...\n  },\n  \"assets\": {\n    \"count\": \"number\",\n    \"facets\": [],\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        ...\n        \"duration\": \"string\",\n        \"exifInfo\": {\n          \"city\": \"string\",\n          \"country\": \"string\",\n          ...\n        },\n        \"fileCreatedAt\": \"string\",\n        \"fileModifiedAt\": \"string\",\n        \"hasMetadata\": \"boolean\",\n        ...\n      }\n    ],\n    \"nextPage\": \"string\",\n    \"total\": \"number\"\n  }\n}\n","json",[26,145,146,151,156,161,166,171,176,180,185,190,195,200,206,212,218,224,230,236,242,248,254,259,265,271,277,283,289],{"__ignoreMap":51},[55,147,148],{"class":57,"line":58},[55,149,150],{},"{\n",[55,152,153],{"class":57,"line":68},[55,154,155],{},"  \"albums\": {\n",[55,157,158],{"class":57,"line":74},[55,159,160],{},"    \"count\": \"number\",\n",[55,162,163],{"class":57,"line":80},[55,164,165],{},"    ...\n",[55,167,168],{"class":57,"line":86},[55,169,170],{},"  },\n",[55,172,173],{"class":57,"line":92},[55,174,175],{},"  \"assets\": {\n",[55,177,178],{"class":57,"line":98},[55,179,160],{},[55,181,182],{"class":57,"line":104},[55,183,184],{},"    \"facets\": [],\n",[55,186,187],{"class":57,"line":110},[55,188,189],{},"    \"items\": [\n",[55,191,192],{"class":57,"line":116},[55,193,194],{},"      {\n",[55,196,197],{"class":57,"line":122},[55,198,199],{},"        ...\n",[55,201,203],{"class":57,"line":202},12,[55,204,205],{},"        \"duration\": \"string\",\n",[55,207,209],{"class":57,"line":208},13,[55,210,211],{},"        \"exifInfo\": {\n",[55,213,215],{"class":57,"line":214},14,[55,216,217],{},"          \"city\": \"string\",\n",[55,219,221],{"class":57,"line":220},15,[55,222,223],{},"          \"country\": \"string\",\n",[55,225,227],{"class":57,"line":226},16,[55,228,229],{},"          ...\n",[55,231,233],{"class":57,"line":232},17,[55,234,235],{},"        },\n",[55,237,239],{"class":57,"line":238},18,[55,240,241],{},"        \"fileCreatedAt\": \"string\",\n",[55,243,245],{"class":57,"line":244},19,[55,246,247],{},"        \"fileModifiedAt\": \"string\",\n",[55,249,251],{"class":57,"line":250},20,[55,252,253],{},"        \"hasMetadata\": \"boolean\",\n",[55,255,257],{"class":57,"line":256},21,[55,258,199],{},[55,260,262],{"class":57,"line":261},22,[55,263,264],{},"      }\n",[55,266,268],{"class":57,"line":267},23,[55,269,270],{},"    ],\n",[55,272,274],{"class":57,"line":273},24,[55,275,276],{},"    \"nextPage\": \"string\",\n",[55,278,280],{"class":57,"line":279},25,[55,281,282],{},"    \"total\": \"number\"\n",[55,284,286],{"class":57,"line":285},26,[55,287,288],{},"  }\n",[55,290,292],{"class":57,"line":291},27,[55,293,294],{},"}\n",[11,296,297,298,301],{},"Now I instantly see that ",[26,299,300],{},"assets.items[i].exifInfo.country"," is a string. That's exactly what I needed to know to map photos by country.",[38,303,305],{"id":304},"extending-it-for-sample-values","Extending it for sample values",[11,307,308],{},"Next, I wondered: what if I wanted real examples, not just types? I modified the primitive case to return the value itself:",[46,310,312],{"className":48,"code":311,"language":50,"meta":51,"style":51},"jq '\ndef shape_with_samples:\n  if type == \"array\" then\n    if length > 0 then [ (.[0] | shape_with_samples) ] else [] end\n  elif type == \"object\" then\n    with_entries(.value |= shape_with_samples)\n  else\n    .\n  end;\nshape_with_samples\n' response.json\n",[26,313,314,320,325,329,334,338,343,347,352,356,361],{"__ignoreMap":51},[55,315,316,318],{"class":57,"line":58},[55,317,23],{"class":61},[55,319,65],{"class":64},[55,321,322],{"class":57,"line":68},[55,323,324],{"class":64},"def shape_with_samples:\n",[55,326,327],{"class":57,"line":74},[55,328,77],{"class":64},[55,330,331],{"class":57,"line":80},[55,332,333],{"class":64},"    if length > 0 then [ (.[0] | shape_with_samples) ] else [] end\n",[55,335,336],{"class":57,"line":86},[55,337,89],{"class":64},[55,339,340],{"class":57,"line":92},[55,341,342],{"class":64},"    with_entries(.value |= shape_with_samples)\n",[55,344,345],{"class":57,"line":98},[55,346,101],{"class":64},[55,348,349],{"class":57,"line":104},[55,350,351],{"class":64},"    .\n",[55,353,354],{"class":57,"line":110},[55,355,113],{"class":64},[55,357,358],{"class":57,"line":116},[55,359,360],{"class":64},"shape_with_samples\n",[55,362,363,365],{"class":57,"line":122},[55,364,125],{"class":64},[55,366,128],{"class":64},[11,368,369],{},"Now I get sample data like:",[46,371,373],{"className":141,"code":372,"language":143,"meta":51,"style":51},"{\n  \"albums\": {\n    \"count\": 10,\n    ...\n  },\n  \"assets\": {\n    \"count\": 25,\n    \"facets\": [],\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        ...\n        \"duration\": \"00:00:05\",\n        \"exifInfo\": {\n          \"city\": \"Zurich\",\n          \"country\": \"Switzerland\"\n        },\n        \"fileCreatedAt\": \"2025-09-01T10:00:00Z\",\n        \"fileModifiedAt\": \"2025-09-01T10:05:00Z\",\n        \"hasMetadata\": true,\n        ...\n      }\n    ],\n    \"nextPage\": \"2\",\n    \"total\": 25\n  }\n}\n",[26,374,375,379,383,388,392,396,400,405,409,413,417,421,426,430,435,440,444,449,454,459,463,467,471,476,481,485],{"__ignoreMap":51},[55,376,377],{"class":57,"line":58},[55,378,150],{},[55,380,381],{"class":57,"line":68},[55,382,155],{},[55,384,385],{"class":57,"line":74},[55,386,387],{},"    \"count\": 10,\n",[55,389,390],{"class":57,"line":80},[55,391,165],{},[55,393,394],{"class":57,"line":86},[55,395,170],{},[55,397,398],{"class":57,"line":92},[55,399,175],{},[55,401,402],{"class":57,"line":98},[55,403,404],{},"    \"count\": 25,\n",[55,406,407],{"class":57,"line":104},[55,408,184],{},[55,410,411],{"class":57,"line":110},[55,412,189],{},[55,414,415],{"class":57,"line":116},[55,416,194],{},[55,418,419],{"class":57,"line":122},[55,420,199],{},[55,422,423],{"class":57,"line":202},[55,424,425],{},"        \"duration\": \"00:00:05\",\n",[55,427,428],{"class":57,"line":208},[55,429,211],{},[55,431,432],{"class":57,"line":214},[55,433,434],{},"          \"city\": \"Zurich\",\n",[55,436,437],{"class":57,"line":220},[55,438,439],{},"          \"country\": \"Switzerland\"\n",[55,441,442],{"class":57,"line":226},[55,443,235],{},[55,445,446],{"class":57,"line":232},[55,447,448],{},"        \"fileCreatedAt\": \"2025-09-01T10:00:00Z\",\n",[55,450,451],{"class":57,"line":238},[55,452,453],{},"        \"fileModifiedAt\": \"2025-09-01T10:05:00Z\",\n",[55,455,456],{"class":57,"line":244},[55,457,458],{},"        \"hasMetadata\": true,\n",[55,460,461],{"class":57,"line":250},[55,462,199],{},[55,464,465],{"class":57,"line":256},[55,466,264],{},[55,468,469],{"class":57,"line":261},[55,470,270],{},[55,472,473],{"class":57,"line":267},[55,474,475],{},"    \"nextPage\": \"2\",\n",[55,477,478],{"class":57,"line":273},[55,479,480],{},"    \"total\": 25\n",[55,482,483],{"class":57,"line":279},[55,484,288],{},[55,486,487],{"class":57,"line":285},[55,488,294],{},[11,490,491,492,495],{},"Seeing ",[26,493,494],{},"\"Switzerland\""," immediately confirmed I was pulling the right field.",[38,497,499],{"id":498},"sampling-the-first-few-items","Sampling the first few items",[11,501,502],{},"When the first asset lacked optional tags, I extended the function to sample the first N items:",[46,504,506],{"className":48,"code":505,"language":50,"meta":51,"style":51},"jq '\ndef shape_with_samples(n):\n  if type == \"array\" then\n    if length > 0 then\n      [ .[:n][] | shape_with_samples(n) ]\n    else [] end\n  elif type == \"object\" then\n    with_entries(.value |= shape_with_samples(n))\n  else\n    .\n  end;\nshape_with_samples(3)\n' response.json\n",[26,507,508,514,519,523,528,533,538,542,547,551,555,559,564],{"__ignoreMap":51},[55,509,510,512],{"class":57,"line":58},[55,511,23],{"class":61},[55,513,65],{"class":64},[55,515,516],{"class":57,"line":68},[55,517,518],{"class":64},"def shape_with_samples(n):\n",[55,520,521],{"class":57,"line":74},[55,522,77],{"class":64},[55,524,525],{"class":57,"line":80},[55,526,527],{"class":64},"    if length > 0 then\n",[55,529,530],{"class":57,"line":86},[55,531,532],{"class":64},"      [ .[:n][] | shape_with_samples(n) ]\n",[55,534,535],{"class":57,"line":92},[55,536,537],{"class":64},"    else [] end\n",[55,539,540],{"class":57,"line":98},[55,541,89],{"class":64},[55,543,544],{"class":57,"line":104},[55,545,546],{"class":64},"    with_entries(.value |= shape_with_samples(n))\n",[55,548,549],{"class":57,"line":110},[55,550,101],{"class":64},[55,552,553],{"class":57,"line":116},[55,554,351],{"class":64},[55,556,557],{"class":57,"line":122},[55,558,113],{"class":64},[55,560,561],{"class":57,"line":202},[55,562,563],{"class":64},"shape_with_samples(3)\n",[55,565,566,568],{"class":57,"line":208},[55,567,125],{"class":64},[55,569,128],{"class":64},[38,571,573],{"id":572},"making-it-reusable","Making it reusable",[11,575,576],{},"I will definitely not remember these functions in a month, so I saved them as reusable scripts:",[46,578,580],{"className":48,"code":579,"language":50,"meta":51,"style":51},"~\u002F.jq\u002Fshape.jq\n~\u002F.jq\u002Fshape_with_samples.jq\n",[26,581,582,592],{"__ignoreMap":51},[55,583,584,588],{"class":57,"line":58},[55,585,587],{"class":586},"szBVR","~",[55,589,591],{"class":590},"sVt8B","\u002F.jq\u002Fshape.jq\n",[55,593,594,596],{"class":57,"line":68},[55,595,587],{"class":586},[55,597,598],{"class":590},"\u002F.jq\u002Fshape_with_samples.jq\n",[11,600,601],{},"Now I can run them anytime via:",[46,603,605],{"className":48,"code":604,"language":50,"meta":51,"style":51},"jq -f ~\u002F.jq\u002Fshape.jq response.json\njq -f ~\u002F.jq\u002Fshape_with_samples.jq response.json\n",[26,606,607,620],{"__ignoreMap":51},[55,608,609,611,615,618],{"class":57,"line":58},[55,610,23],{"class":61},[55,612,614],{"class":613},"sj4cs"," -f",[55,616,617],{"class":64}," ~\u002F.jq\u002Fshape.jq",[55,619,128],{"class":64},[55,621,622,624,626,629],{"class":57,"line":68},[55,623,23],{"class":61},[55,625,614],{"class":613},[55,627,628],{"class":64}," ~\u002F.jq\u002Fshape_with_samples.jq",[55,630,128],{"class":64},[38,632,634],{"id":633},"conclusion","Conclusion",[11,636,637],{},"It’s a simple trick, but it makes large JSON responses much easier to read. When you hit an undocumented API, jq maps its structure fast and without guesswork.",[639,640,641],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sScJk, html code.shiki .sScJk{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .sZZnC, html code.shiki .sZZnC{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}html.dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}html pre.shiki code .szBVR, html code.shiki .szBVR{--shiki-default:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583}html pre.shiki code .sVt8B, html code.shiki .sVt8B{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .sj4cs, html code.shiki .sj4cs{--shiki-default:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF}",{"title":51,"searchDepth":68,"depth":68,"links":643},[644,645,646,647,648,649],{"id":40,"depth":68,"text":41},{"id":134,"depth":68,"text":135},{"id":304,"depth":68,"text":305},{"id":498,"depth":68,"text":499},{"id":572,"depth":68,"text":573},{"id":633,"depth":68,"text":634},"Use jq to automatically map and visualize the structure of large JSON responses, perfect for exploring undocumented endpoints.","md","\u002Fimages\u002Fjq-json-structure.webp",{},true,null,"\u002Fblog\u002Fjq-json-outline","2025-10-19",false,{"title":5,"description":650},{"loc":656},"blog\u002Fjq-json-outline",[23,143,663,664,665],"command line","automation","developer productivity","-PixPFYLZb1Shr6vgOlbyEYvBygB3oGIny9z0Ln_b8Y",[668,678,688,694,702,704,713,722,728,734,743,750,756,763],{"title":669,"description":670,"tags":671,"postDate":676,"path":677,"url":655},"Stop stashing half-finished work: use Git worktrees and Worktrunk","Git worktrees keep separate branches checked out at once. Worktrunk automates per-worktree setup. The same isolation also works for parallel AI agents.",[672,673,674,665,663,675],"git","worktrees","worktrunk","workflow","2026-08-16","\u002Fblog\u002Fworktrees-with-worktrunk",{"title":679,"description":680,"tags":681,"postDate":686,"path":687,"url":655},"Self-Hosting my Git forge with Forgejo","Why I moved away from GitHub and chose a lightweight, community-driven alternative",[682,683,684,685],"Homelab","Open source","Self-hosting","Workflow","2026-04-29","\u002Fblog\u002Fself-hosting-my-git-forge",{"title":689,"description":690,"tags":691,"postDate":692,"path":693,"url":655},"Curating my own reading and discovery feed with RSS","Taking concrete steps away from algorithms using FreshRSS, self-hosted tools, and a pipeline built for me.",[682,683,684,685],"2026-02-08","\u002Fblog\u002Freading-and-discovery-feed-curation",{"title":695,"description":696,"tags":697,"postDate":700,"path":701,"url":655},"Fixing my broken Docker Immich+Traefik setup","Photo indexing failed in my Immich+Traefik setup. I'd misconfigured my Docker networking. Here's how I figured it out and what I changed.",[698,699],"homelab","networking","2025-10-31","\u002Fb